# Binaries
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary
*.test

# Output of go coverage tool
*.out
*.prof

# Build / docs artifacts
dist/
site/
*.sarif

# Dependency directories
vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Editor artifacts
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS artifacts
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test output, and every real .evtx a developer keeps locally.
testdata/*.evtx
# One exception: a log this project generated on a Windows machine it
# controls, committed so CI can check the chunk hash-table rules against real
# Windows output again. It is a CI fixture, NOT a source of format rules —
# rules are derived from the corpus census, never from one file. That
# distinction is what the deleted testdata/system.evtx got wrong.
!testdata/win2025-system.evtx
